# EtIllustration

Renders Design System illustrations from Figma
([Illustrations — Images — 2026](https://www.figma.com/design/dbI2fqZ3Gngs1PWBawWEXu/Illustrations---Images---2026?node-id=226-36472)).

Assets live on the CDN under
`https://etoro-cdn.etorostatic.com/web-client/et-plus/etoro/illustrations/`
as `{name}_{size}_{theme}.{png|svg}`. The component loads them with `expo-image`
via `getIllustrationUrl` — no local SVG/PNG baking at runtime.

Theme is resolved from `useEtoroTheme().dark` unless `theme` is passed explicitly.
Both light and dark CDN files MUST exist for every registered base and size-variant
key listed in `ILLUSTRATION_META` / `ILLUSTRATION_ASSET_FORMAT`.

## Usage

```tsx
import { EtIllustration } from 'etoro-ui';

<EtIllustration name="error" size="m" />
<EtIllustration name="paper_plane" size="xxl" />
<EtIllustration name="success" size="xl" theme="dark" />
```

## Props

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `name` | `IllustrationName` | required | Kebab-case Figma illustration name |
| `size` | `'s' \| 'm' \| 'xl' \| 'xxl'` | Figma native size for `name` | Loads a size-specific CDN variant if one exists, else scales the base asset to fit the token box |
| `theme` | `'light' \| 'dark'` | from app theme | Force light/dark asset |
| `width` / `height` | `number` | intrinsic | Optional overrides (aspect ratio preserved if one set) |
| `testID` | `string` | — | Test id |
| `accessibilityLabel` | `string` | `name` | A11y label |

## Size tokens (Figma)

Every illustration has a **base** CDN asset per theme. By default `size` scales that
asset to *fit* the token's nominal box (aspect preserved). The default per illustration
is its Figma native size in `ILLUSTRATION_META[name].defaultSize` (e.g. `coupon` → `s`,
status icons → `m`, coast-to-coast → `xxl`).

**Size-specific variants**: some illustrations also ship a dedicated asset for a given
size — a genuinely different layout. Passing that `size` loads the variant URL instead
of scaling the base. Current variants:
- **Status set** (`error`, `success`, `connection_error`, `warning`, `pending`) — wide **XL**

Dedicated variants render at their own intrinsic dimensions from
`ILLUSTRATION_META[name].variants[size]`.

| Token | Nominal box | Typical use |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `s` | 124×124 | CMS / cards |
| `m` | 152×152 | Drawer / empty |
| `xl` | 375×158 | Status banners |
| `xxl` | 375×230 | UX / screens (coast-to-coast) |

## CDN assets & formats

- **URL**: `{cdn}/etoro/illustrations/{name}_{assetSize}_{theme}.{format}`
- **Format map**: `illustration-assets.generated.ts` (`ILLUSTRATION_ASSET_FORMAT`)
  — `png` for illustrations that need `feTurbulence` stipple/glow (native RN-SVG cannot
  render it); `svg` for flat line art.
- **Meta**: `illustration-meta.ts` — `defaultSize`, intrinsic dims, optional `variants`.
- **Resolver**: `utils/get-illustration-url.ts`.

PNG files uploaded to the CDN MUST be **transparent** (no baked `#F5F5F5` canvas).
Export SVG from Figma, strip the background/annotation rects, then bake through
headless Chromium when `feTurbulence` is present — never use Figma's opaque PNG export
for dark surfaces.

To add/update an illustration:

1. Upload light + dark files to the CDN with the `name_size_theme` naming.
2. Add/update `ILLUSTRATION_META` and `ILLUSTRATION_ASSET_FORMAT` (and `IllustrationName` if new).
3. Cover the new URL/size behavior in `et-illustration.test.tsx`.

